      {
        "id": "proj-snow-battle",
        "title": "Snow Battle",
        "sections": [
          {
            "id": "description",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Developed from a more open-ended prompt in the Game Development course, this project came from the initiative to explore topics beyond the traditional syllabus, with an experimental focus on 2D multiplayer over a local network (LAN) via IP. In Godot with GDScript, the prototype investigates structuring network sessions, state synchronization, and player movement, applying core multiplayer architecture concepts such as host vs. client distinction, entity replication, and remote message exchange."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "tech",
            "content": [
